            "review_title": "Review at Bà Năm Seafood",
            "review_text": "vbertola\nTurin, Italy163 contributions\n0\nThis place is heaven!\nSep 2023 • Solo\nI stumbled upon it almost by chance, looking for a place to eat that was less touristy and less messy than the stalls at the Son Tra night market; and I ended up going back three times. It's an incredible place: I had three fish and seafood dinners, each more exceptional than the other. Really: between the three dinners I tried about ten different things and there were perhaps two that were \"only\" excellent, the others were exceptional, truly among the best I've ever eaten in the whole world (and I travel around a lot).\n\nI ate lightly fried or breaded calamari, oysters seasoned with peanuts (extraordinary), a fantastic mackerel baked in foil, little crabs so tender that you could munch on the shell, clams in lemongrass broth, octopus in Thai sauce (spicy!), and a dish of razor clams in satay sauce, strange but excellent. All very fresh, all with a bill of between 10 and 15 euros for dinner.\n\nIf you want, there is also fried rice in a thousand ways, there are rice spaghetti, there are meat dishes in abundance (the menu is endless) but the extraordinary thing here is the seafood. The staff is plentiful and very kind, they communicate without problems, they take credit cards. Plus, it's at the beginning of the dragon bridge, so you can have dinner here and then, from Friday to Sunday, enjoy the amazing dragon fire and water show. I hope to be able to return there sooner or later in life.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten September 11, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
